# Keep the Docker build context lean — without this, every build
# would copy 200+ MB of node_modules and dist into the build context
# (slow + wastes disk).

# ─── never include build artefacts (rebuilt inside container) ───
node_modules
dist
.cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── never include the vendored engine + puzzle DB ──────────────
# These are pulled at build time by `npm run vendor:engine` /
# `npm run build:puzzles`. Including stale local copies would just
# bloat the build context.
public/engine/*.wasm
public/engine/*.nnue
public/engine/*.js
public/puzzles.db

# ─── dev tooling and local state ────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.dev/wsl-*.sh
.claude
.env
.env.*

# ─── tests + docs not needed in production image ────────────────
tests
docs
playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
test-results

# ─── platform / OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─── keep the Dockerfile + compose in context, of course ────────
# (no negation needed — they aren't matched by the rules above)
